<title>LITHUANIA: PREMIER TO ATTEND EU ASSOCIATE MEETING.</title>
<headline>PREMIER TO ATTEND EU ASSOCIATE MEETING.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuanian Prime Minister Gediminas Vagnorius will head a government delegation to the Netherlands on Friday to take part in a meeting of European Union (EU) associate countries, the government said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;During the meeting, European Union President Jacques Santer will inform about the EU Commission's decisions, which were adopted recently at the Intergovernmenal Conference in Amsterdam,&quot; the government' press office said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;EU Associate countries will be familiarised with the European Union's planned institutional reforms, which open the way for EU expansion,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 18</p>
